---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — AirScanner"
  description="How AirScanner handles local scans, scanner connections, optional sharing, and visits to this website."
  legal
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">AirScanner / Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Effective <time datetime="2026-09-28">28 September 2026</time></p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      AirScanner processes scans on your iPhone or iPad. The developer does not
      collect your scanned documents, recognized text, usage analytics, advertising
      identifiers, or app account data. There is no app account, developer backend,
      advertising, analytics SDK, or app-managed cloud sync.
    </p>

    <h2>What your device stores</h2>
    <p>
      The app keeps saved PDFs, document metadata, recognized text used for search
      (OCR), and small settings on your device. OCR runs on-device. Deleting a
      document in the app removes its PDF and OCR index from the app; it does not
      remove copies you previously exported or copies in existing backups.
    </p>
    <p>
      Normal iOS or iPadOS backups can include app data, depending on your system
      settings. Local storage is not a promise that data can never leave your
      device: backups and destinations you choose may store copies elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Connecting to a scanner</h2>
    <p>
      Local Network permission lets AirScanner discover and communicate with
      compatible scanners on your local network. Scan commands and images travel
      between your device and the scanner, not through a developer server.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use a network and scanner you trust. A scanner connection may use unencrypted
      HTTP. For HTTPS connections, trust is scoped to the discovered scanner rather
      than normal public-web certificate validation. AirScanner does not promise
      end-to-end encryption or that a local network is secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Actions you choose</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Sharing and export.</strong> A selected app, service, or file
        destination receives the content you send. Its own privacy rules and sync
        settings apply.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Photos.</strong> Exporting a PDF’s first page to Photos requests
        add-only permission when you choose that action. Photos may sync the image
        according to your Apple settings. AirScanner does not request full
        photo-library read access, camera access, or microphone access.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clipboard.</strong> Text you copy leaves the app’s storage boundary
        and becomes available through the system clipboard, including any
        system-managed clipboard sharing you enable.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ratings.</strong> Optional in-app rating prompts use Apple’s StoreKit
        system. Apple controls that process; the developer receives no in-app
        record of your review response.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>This website and its host</h2>
    <p>
      This is a static website. It adds no analytics, tracking, cookies, contact
      forms, third-party scripts, external fonts, or embedded third-party resources.
      External links load their destination only when you follow them.
    </p>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages hosts this site. GitHub logs and stores visitors’ IP addresses
      for security, including visits made without signing in. See GitHub’s
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">Pages data-collection disclosure</a>
      and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>
      for how GitHub handles that information.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and public support</h2>
    <p>
      For general questions, use the
      <a href="https://github.com/jtvargas/airscanner-web/issues">public website-repository issues</a>.
      Posting is voluntary. Issues are public: maintainers and others can see your
      post and public GitHub account information. GitHub operates this service
      under its own privacy statement linked above.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Do not post scanned documents, personal information, or network
      identifiers</strong> such as IP addresses, Wi-Fi names, or scanner serial
      numbers. Describe the problem without those details.
    </p>

    <h2>Policy updates</h2>
    <p>
      Changes to these practices will be reflected here with an updated effective
      date. This page describes the app and website practices as of the date above.
    </p>
    <p><a href={`${base}terms/`}>Read the terms of use</a> or <a href={base}>return to AirScanner</a>.</p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
